+      "type": "text",
+      "title": "One rule for the mood",
+      "content": "After a reporting verb, ask what follows it:\n\n• **A fact the speaker states: indicative.** *Afirmó que la tienda cerraba a las ocho. Admitió que se había equivocado.* After a past verb the tense moves back, as in B2 Unit 17.\n• **A claim that is rejected: subjunctive.** *Negó que fuera su error.* You know *negar que* + subjunctive from B2 Unit 5.\n• ***Advertir* and *recordar* can report either.** If what follows is a fact, use the indicative: *Me advirtió que el tren salía a las ocho. Me recordó que la reunión era el lunes.* If it is something to do or not to do, use the subjunctive, as for the orders of B1 Unit 38: *Me advirtió que no llegara tarde. Me recordó que cerrara la puerta.*\n• ***Sugerir* and *reprochar* take the subjunctive.** *Sugirió que esperáramos* (a proposal). *Me reprochó que no hubiera llamado* (a blame). For something that was not done, the pluperfect subjunctive is the form you learned in B2 Unit 16."
